// cross_mod_array_arg — regression test for the round-7 fix: an ARRAY
// argument to an imported function must bind (0.7.2's placeholder-based
// guard rejected every array argument to an imported callee). Since the
// v1.12 type descriptors the `int[] a` formal round-trips as a real
// array type — the consumer-side stub rebuilds the true signature, and
// the element reads in this sum come back exact. Guards against both
// the old rejection and silent wrong-kind binding.
int sum(int[] a) {
    int s = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i = i + 1)
        s = s + a[i];
    return s;
}
